# ── INTERPRETATION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# W44-54 DC LearnTree wins are concentrated on screenshot content (terminal,
# imac_g3) where heavily-quantised DC has 0-1 unique values per block —
# the W44-50 forensic analysis predicted exactly this: the fixed WP-BSP
# tree (45 contexts post AC-metadata merge) spends ~4500 bits of ANS
# histogram tables where 1-3 contexts would suffice. The learned tree
# collapses to a few leaves on flat content.
#
# Photo regressions concentrate on smooth content (1418519 uniformly,
# 1189261 partially) where WP-on-DC is a substantially better predictor
# than clamped_gradient — DC residuals have spatial structure that WP
# captures via its multi-channel weighted prediction but gradient does
# not. The 1418519 cluster regression is +1.36 % bytes mean, peaking at
# +2.03 % — consistent with the W44-54 commit's predicted +2-3 % photo
# cluster.
#
# This validates the W44-54 commit's follow-on plan: a WP-residual
# sub-chunk (gather samples on Weighted Predictor residuals + tokenise
# with WP prediction at learned-tree leaves) should recover the smooth-
# photo regression while keeping the screenshot win, since libjxl's
# `Predictor::Variable` (effort >= 4) selects WP per-leaf for DC on
# photo content.

# ── PHOTO REGRESSION ASSESSMENT ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Only 1 of 287 sampled FIXED cells flipped to OPEN (1418519 e9 d=0.8,
# noise-level boundary cross at +1.0 % bytes). No quality regressions
# (bfly_delta_pct and ssim2_delta_abs unchanged on every cell — DC
# re-tokenisation is a pure bitstream-efficiency change).
#
# The 1418519 cluster has +1.36 % bytes mean across all 40 cells, but
# 39 of them were already FIXED at bytes_d% > 1.5 % (smooth-photo
# cluster within tolerance) so only the e9 d=0.8 boundary cell tipped
# over. The remaining 39 are still FIXED at bytes_d% in the 1-2 % range,
# now bumped to ~2-3 % but still under the wedge gate.
#
# Net: NO quality regressions, NO functional regressions, 1 noise-level
# OPEN flip on a smooth-photo cluster (predicted by W44-54), 6 OPEN→FIXED
# wins on screenshot + smooth-photo high-d content.

# ── RECOMMENDED NEXT CHUNK ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Highest-EV follow-on per W44-54 commit message: **WP-residual sub-chunk
# (issue #56 follow-on)**.
#
# Spec:
#   (1) Gather DC samples on Weighted Predictor residuals instead of
#       clamped_gradient residuals.
#   (2) Allow `Predictor::Weighted` (predictor=6) at learned-tree leaves
#       (currently hardcoded to Gradient=5).
#   (3) Tokenise via WP prediction at decode time (decoder reads the
#       per-leaf predictor field, so this is purely encoder-side).
#   (4) Re-include property 15 (`wp_max_error`) in the splitter candidate
#       set — this gives the tree access to WP's per-position confidence,
#       which is the dominant signal on smooth-photo DC where WP wins.
#
# Expected outcome (from W44-54 follow-on + this refresh):
#   - 1418519 cluster regression closes (+1.36 % → ~0 % byte mean)
#   - 1189261 partial cluster closes (+0.41 % → ~0 %)
#   - Screenshot wins preserved (terminal −2.4 %, imac_g3 −1.2 %)
#   - 1418519 e9 d=0.8 flip-back FIXED→FIXED (regression source removed)
#
# If WP-residual sub-chunk lands cleanly: estimate ledger drops from
# 26 OPEN to ~22-23 OPEN (1418519 cells were not OPEN to begin with —
# the win on them is metric-internal, not flip-producing — but combined
# with screenshot wins continuing to flip the next-marginal OPEN cells,
# net flip count ~3-4 additional OPEN→FIXED expected).
#
# Pivot signal: if codec_wiki cells (currently 5 OPEN at e7) did NOT
# close further — they didn't (codec_wiki e7 d=3/4/5/6 all still OPEN,
# byte changes flat at +0.08 % mean across the image). codec_wiki wedge
# is NOT in the DC-LearnTree EV path — it's a per-section attribution
# question already filed at W44-42 (rqwkrrpqswxk). Defer.
#
# Per-image OPEN counts after W44-55:
#   1420710  10 OPEN (high-d photo, F-D cluster, NOT addressable by DC tree)
#   1531677   6 OPEN (high-d photo, partially addressed; 4 more flipped this chunk)
#   1189261   4 OPEN (mid-d photo, F-D cluster)
#   codec_wiki 4 OPEN (e7 d=3,4,5,6 — block context map count wedge per W44-39/W44-42)
#   1418519   1 OPEN (NEW, sub-threshold smooth-photo regression, will close with WP)
#   1025469   1 OPEN (boundary cell)
#   terminal  0 OPEN (was 1, W44-50 wedge CLOSED)
#   imac_g3   0 OPEN
#
# So the 26 remaining OPEN cells split:
#   - 20 high-d photo cells (F-D cluster, NOT DC-tree addressable, need
#     quant-field / LF quant work per W44-47 recommendation)
#   - 4 codec_wiki e7 cells (block context map, separate wedge)
#   - 2 boundary noise cells (will fluctuate with any bitstream change)
#
# WP-residual sub-chunk is the right next move because it both
# (a) makes the W44-54 DC LearnTree net-positive on photos (closes the
# 1418519 cluster regression), and (b) leaves the F-D photo cluster
# work (W44-47 recommended chunk) as the next-priority follow-on after
# WP-residual lands.
